 keep their existing meanings. No cross-packet dictionary or retained decoding
 state is needed.
 
+The reserved tag `0x53`, with bit 7 supplying sign, stores one of two related
+nonzero Session identifiers. The fixed uint32 transform is `x ^= x << 13;
+x ^= x >> 17; x ^= x << 5`. A second byte carries direction in bit 4 and the
+number of steps minus one in bits 5–7. The explicit identifier predicts the other
+one in one to eight steps. Both complete identifiers are reconstructed; other
+pairs keep the literal layout.
+
+The descriptor's low bits announce anchor start, anchor diff, start delta and
+magnitude, respectively. Anchor diff defaults to one; the start delta retains
+zigzag encoding. One shared last-pair cache includes unsuccessful searches and
+does not depend on Projection lifetime. This form always saves three bytes.
+Snapshot dictionaries and mask batches retain their existing layouts.
+
